SUMMARY:Spring Concert: The Ripple Effect
DESCRIPTION:The Pamela Trokanski Dance Theatre invites the community to join them for the premiere of The Ripple Effect\, a thoughtful and sometimes humorous exploration of the repercussions of our actions as individuals\, communities\, and as a species.\nJoining PTDT are the PTDT Apprentice Company\, Light Ballet Company\, and The Third Stage. Known for work that integrates a strong sense of athleticism and technical training with idiosyncratic movements and a diverse range of movers\, including dancers ranging in age from 10 to 90+\, this is not your average dance performance!\nThe performance will open on Sat\, April 25 @ 6pm\, and will follow up with a matinee on Sun\, April 26 @ 2pm.\nAll performances are held at the Louise H. Kellogg Memorial Theater\, located at the Pamela Trokanski Dance Workshop\, 2720 Del Rio Place\, in Davis.\nTickets are available in advance and at the door: $20 – General Admission / $15 – Children\, Students\, Adults 65+\nFor more information or to purchase tickets\, please call (530)756-3949 or email office@trokanski.com\nThis concert has been funded\, in part\, by Douglas Neuhauser\, Kimberly Baxter\, and Lisa DeAmicis & Thomas S. Nesbitt. \n 
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/spring-concert-the-ripple-effect/2026-04-26/
LOCATION:Louise H Kellogg Memorial Theater at the Pamela Trokanski Dance Workshop\, 2720 Del Rio Place\, Davis\, CA\, 95618\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bring the Kids,Community,Stage & Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Poster-for-Davis-Dirt.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Pamela Trokanski Dance Theatre":MAILTO:office@trokanski.com
END:VEVENT
